    "message": "Move the movement rules of a tick into Rust\n\nadvance_movement, start_movement, finish_movement, route_with_movement_time,\nroute_is_physically_clear, plan_in_room_route, _queue_slot_position,\nfacility_approach_route and the movement_v1 validation run on the row, and a\nfloor plan is read as data. A tick where a queue trip must replan or a person is\nplaced in a queue slot in the walk goes to the Python rule, because those depend\non the order of the walk. Queue scheduling stays in Python.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
